{
  "_about": [
    "Golden cases for the history share lane frame, its chunking arithmetic, and which words may fill a message's seat.",
    "Normative: docs/sealed-messages.md §History shares.",
    "`parse`: `wire` is the decrypted application payload. `expect` is null when it is not a share (never an error: an unknown payload is ignored), or the fields a reader may use: share, chunk, chunks, window, for, with, and the surviving messages. A message entry missing an id, an author or a timestamp is dropped and the rest of the share still parses. Unknown keys are ignored at both levels.",
    "`version` 2 is the only version, and a share MUST carry `\"to\": \"person\"`.",
    "A share for several people names the first in `for` and all of them in `with`, written only when there is more than one. A reader's recipients are `with`'s non-empty strings, once each, in order, with `for` first when the list leaves it out; with no `with` (or one that is not an array) they are just `for`. In a parse `expect`, absent `with` is [`for`], or [] for an empty `for`.",
    "Entries carry the frame's optional `i`, `r` and `b`, read with the frame's rules; a bad one never drops the entry. In `expect`, an absent `clientId`, `replyTo` or `broadcast` means \"\", \"\" or false.",
    "`cost` and `chunk`: the split is arithmetic on UTF-8 byte counts, never on a serialized length, so that every language splits the same way. cost(m) = utf8(m.id) + utf8(m.by) + 2 * utf8(m.text) + `entryOverheadBytes`, plus utf8(i) + utf8(r) when present. A chunk holds messages while `envelopeOverheadBytes` + sum(cost) <= the budget, and never holds none: one oversized message rides alone. The cases use small budgets so the arithmetic is readable; the real budget is `maxChunkBytes`.",
    "`roundTrip`: the messages written must read back equal, thread keys and recipients included.",
    "`seat`: whether words arriving for a message's seat may replace what is held. `held` is null (no row and no words), `unread` (a message this device was sent and could not open), `author` (the author's own words) or `quotation` (a history share); `incoming` is `author` or `quotation`. The author's own words always store; a quotation only fills a seat that holds nothing, never one this device was sent.",
    "`admit`: whether a shared message may make a seat at all: only when its `at` falls in a whole second strictly earlier than the second of `joinedAt`, when this device joined the group (null when unknown, which admits nothing). Both are the server's time to the second; the millisecond of `at` is only the sharer's delivery order. Other entries are dropped and the rest of the share still files.",
    "`joinLine`: the `joinedAt` that `admit` takes: `latest`, the server time of the Welcome that seated this device most recently (a re-add or a rejoin is a later Welcome), else `first`, the first join kept, else `registered`, this device's registration time; null when none is known, and then the share is not dropped but read again later.",
    "`share`: the whole decision for one entry: `admit` against `joinLine` (`first`, `latest`, `registered`), and an `at` in a whole second later than `heldBefore`, the newest row the device holds in the conversation from before the line that is not a quotation, rows a hand-off from the account's own devices carried included (null when it holds none). A share never writes in among history the device holds, whatever its first join.",
    "`recheck`: after a history transfer imports rows into a conversation, its quotations are checked again against the new `heldBefore`, and every one in a whole second at or before it is deleted, whichever arrived first. `rows` are the conversation's rows, `line` is `joinLine`, and `expect` is the ids deleted, in row order. A held quotation the transfer carries is replaced by its copy, which is then held.",
    "Object keys and ids in these cases are opaque test strings; a reader does not interpret them beyond the rules cited above.",
    "To replay: run each case through your own implementation of the format and compare the result with the case's expectation, field by field."
  ],
  "version": 2,
  "maxChunkBytes": 131072,
  "entryOverheadBytes": 64,
  "envelopeOverheadBytes": 256,
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "an ordinary sentence is not a bundle",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "shall we ask something about the ferry times",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "json that is not ours is not a bundle",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"something-else\",\"v\":1}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "version 2 that does not say who it is for is not a bundle it may read",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"history\",\"v\":2,\"share\":\"s1\",\"chunk\":0,\"chunks\":1,\"window\":\"everything\",\"for\":\"\",\"messages\":[]}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "version 2 naming a recipient other than a person is a later format, not a guess",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"history\",\"v\":2,\"to\":\"assistant\",\"share\":\"s1\",\"chunk\":0,\"chunks\":1,\"window\":\"everything\",\"for\":\"actor-bob\",\"messages\":[]}",
      "expect": null
    },
    {
      "name": "a version this build does not know is not a bundle it may read",
      "call": "parse",
      "wire": "{\"peachy\":\"history\",\"v\":3,\"to\":\"person\",\"share\":\"s1\",\"chunk\":0,\"chunks\":1,\"window\":\"everything\",\"for\":\"actor-bob\",\"messages\":[]}",
      "expect": null
    },
